@startuml 05-state-payment
title PayLink - Payment Life Cycle State Diagram
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Initiated : payment created

state Initiated
state FundsHeld
state SentToBiller
state Unknown
state Failed
state Completed <<final>>
state Rejected <<final>>
state Refunded <<final>>

Initiated --> FundsHeld : fraud checks pass &\nsufficient available balance
Initiated --> Rejected : fraud check fails,\nbill amount mismatch or\ninsufficient funds

FundsHeld --> SentToBiller : payment request sent\nto biller with reference

SentToBiller --> Completed : biller confirms payment
SentToBiller --> Failed : biller refuses payment
SentToBiller --> Unknown : timeout (>10s) or\nasync pending (TopUpNet)

Unknown --> Completed : later confirmation\n(callback / retry / settlement)
Unknown --> Failed : later refusal or\nnot found in settlement

Failed --> Refunded : held funds released\nto wallet via ledger

Completed --> [*]
Rejected --> [*]
Refunded --> [*]

note right of Unknown
  - Money stays in HELD balance.
  - Re-queried after 1, 5 and 15 min (config),
    then checked in reconciliation.
  - Applies to timeouts AND TopUpNet async payments
    (a callback may resolve it earlier).
  - NEVER auto-refunded while Unknown.
end note

note left of FundsHeld
  Crash recovery (no extra states):
  - stuck in FundsHeld -> resume: send to the biller
    with the SAME reference (idempotent at biller).
  - stuck in SentToBiller -> query(reference):
    PAID -> Completed, FAILED -> Failed, no answer -> Unknown.
end note

note bottom of Completed
  Completed stays Completed even after a refund.
  A refund of a Completed payment is a RefundRequest +
  REFUND / COMMISSION_REVERSAL ledger entries, not a state change.
end note
@enduml
